Package: scelo
Type: Package
Title: Soft Data, Tools, Hard Data: The Scelo Workbench for Actuaries Who Write Code
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ali", "Denewade", email = "scelo@intelligentactuaries.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Intelligent Actuaries (Pty) Ltd", role = c("cph", "fnd")))
Description: The Scelo IDE's brain layer as an R package: the same import typing,
    cleaning rules, life tables, commutation functions, reserving engine (chain
    ladder, Mack, Bornhuetter-Ferguson, ODP bootstrap), discount curves, Smith-Wilson,
    aggregate-loss models, credibility, GLM relativities, fairness audits and the
    W(M,T,R) survival forecast that the desktop workbench runs, plus a client for
    the bundled decision-support swarm. Every function takes a data frame first,
    infers the columns it needs from their names, and returns a table that carries
    its basis, its caveats and, once stamped, a content hash: numbers that travel
    with their provenance. Base R only; optional packages add speed and extras.
